      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see that you\u0027ve move existing parameters around in `parse_iommus` and `parse` so the above was probably not clear. My point was that, as you\u0027re extending\n```\nDeviceAssignmentInfo::parse(\u0026Fdt, \u0026VmDtbo)\n```\nby adding a new `hypervisor` parameter as the last parameter:\n```\nDeviceAssignmentInfo::parse(\u0026Fdt, \u0026VmDtbo, \u0026dyn DeviceAssigningHypervisor)\n```\nit might be clearer to be consistent and extend other existing methods in the same way.\n\nThat is, from\n```\nAssignedDeviceInfo {\n    parse(\u0026Fdt, \u0026VmDtbo, \u0026CStr, \u0026BTreeMap\u003c_, _\u003e)\n    parse_iommus(\u0026FdtNode, \u0026BTreeMap\u003c_, _\u003e)\n}\n```\nto\n```\nAssignedDeviceInfo {\n    parse(\u0026Fdt, \u0026VmDtbo, \u0026CStr, \u0026BTreeMap\u003c_, _\u003e, \u0026dyn DeviceAssigningHypervisor)\n    parse_iommus(\u0026FdtNode, \u0026BTreeMap\u003c_, _\u003e, \u0026dyn DeviceAssigningHypervisor)\n    parse_reg(\u0026FdtNode, \u0026dyn DeviceAssigningHypervisor)\n}\n```\nnot (as we currently have in PS13)\n```\nAssignedDeviceInfo {\n    parse(\u0026Fdt, \u0026VmDtbo, \u0026dyn DeviceAssigningHypervisor, \u0026BTreeMap\u003c_, _\u003e, \u0026CStr)\n    parse_iommus(\u0026dyn DeviceAssigningHypervisor, \u0026BTreeMap\u003c_, _\u003e, \u0026FdtNode)\n    parse_reg(\u0026dyn DeviceAssigningHypervisor, \u0026FdtNode)\n}\n```",
