      "writtenOn": "2023-11-28T11:42:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I love this, we could do so much more testing-wise for pvmfw by building on this idea!\n\nMay I recommend we make the mock hypervisor fully configurable from the test itself i.e. no implicit results (such as the `Ok(0)` currently in `::new`)?\n\nFor example, the MMIO interface could be (untested but you get the idea):\n```\nstruct MockHypervisor {\n    mmio_tokens: hyp::Result\u003cHashMap::\u003c(u64, u64), u64\u003e\u003e,\n}\n\nimpl MockHypervisor {\n    fn new() -\u003e Self {\n        Self { mmio_tokens: Ok(HashMap::new()) }\n    }\n\n    fn insert_mmio_token(\u0026mut self, ipa: u64, size: u64, pa: u64) {\n        if let Ok(ref mut tokens) \u003d self.mmio_tokens {\n            tokens.insert((ipa, size), pa);\n        } // This ignores Err() but we could also unwrap.\n    }\n\n    fn force_error_get_phys_mmio_token(\u0026mut self, e: hyp::Error) {\n        self.mmio_tokens \u003d Err(e);\n    }\n}\n\nimpl DeviceAssigningHypervisor for MockHypervisor {\n    fn get_phys_mmio_token(\u0026self, ipa: u64, size: u64) -\u003e hyp::Result\u003cu64\u003e {\n        let tokens \u003d self.mmio_tokens.as_ref()?;\n\n        tokens.get((ipa, size)).cloned().ok_or(Err(\n            hyp::Error::KvmError(\n                hyp::KvmError::InvalidParameter,\n                0xc6000012, /* VENDOR_HYP_KVM_DEV_REQ_MMIO_FUNC_ID */\n            )\n        )\n    }\n}\n```\n(and exact same approach for pvIOMMUs), which would allow tests to configure the mock as they please before passing it to the function-under-test while somehow mimicking the actual EL2 implementation. AFAICT, this API would fit _any_ test-case, including those covering PA mismatches, which are currently missing.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 498,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 501,
        "endChar": 5
      },
